Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

• races  
  – race_id : join‑key to results (and other sporting tables)  
  – year    : restrict to seasons 1950‑1959  
  – round   : chronological order inside one season  

• results  
  – race_id        : join to races to know the season / round  
  – driver_id      : the person we analyse  
  – constructor_id : team that built the car (we must compare first vs. last)  

• drivers  
  – driver_id  : join to results  
  – forename / surname / full_name : show readable driver names  

The logic to answer the question  

For every (driver , season‑year) in 1950‑1959  
  1. Collect all the rounds he actually started (≥ 2 distinct rounds).  
  2. Determine the constructor used in his first round of that year (smallest round).  
  3. Determine the constructor used in his last round of that year (largest round).  
  4. Keep the driver if the constructor in step‑2 equals the constructor in step‑3.  

Below are 10 exploratory SQL queries (from simple inspection to the final answer).  
All queries are written for SQLite; table / column names are wrapped in double quotes only when necessary.  
Each query returns at most 20 rows with DISTINCT where it makes sense.

```sql
-- 1. Distinct years that exist in the raw "races" table (to confirm the 1950‑1959 span is available)
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM races
WHERE year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Sample of 1950s races with their basic information
SELECT race_id, year, round, name, date
FROM races
WHERE year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
ORDER BY year, round
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. All drivers that have at least one classified result in the 1950s
SELECT DISTINCT r.driver_id
FROM results AS r
JOIN races  AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
WHERE ra.year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Attach driver names to those IDs for human readability
SELECT DISTINCT d.driver_id,
       d.forename || ' ' || d.surname AS driver_name
FROM results  AS r
JOIN races    AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
JOIN drivers  AS d  ON d.driver_id = r.driver_id
WHERE ra.year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Show (race_id, year, round, driver_id, constructor_id) sample to inspect data we will aggregate
SELECT ra.year, ra.round, r.driver_id, r.constructor_id
FROM results AS r
JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
WHERE ra.year = 1950
ORDER BY r.driver_id, ra.round
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Count how many distinct rounds each driver entered in every 1950s season
SELECT r.driver_id,
       ra.year,
       COUNT(DISTINCT ra.round) AS rounds_entered
FROM results AS r
JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
WHERE ra.year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
GROUP BY r.driver_id, ra.year
HAVING rounds_entered >= 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Determine the constructor used in the first round of each (driver, year)
SELECT t.driver_id,
       t.year,
       MIN(t.round) AS first_round,
       MAX(t.round) AS last_round
FROM (
    SELECT r.driver_id,
           ra.year,
           ra.round
    FROM results AS r
    JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
    WHERE ra.year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
) AS t
GROUP BY t.driver_id, t.year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Find first‑race constructor for every (driver, year)
SELECT s.driver_id,
       s.year,
       r.constructor_id AS first_constructor_id
FROM (
    SELECT driver_id, year, MIN(round) AS first_round
    FROM (
        SELECT r.driver_id, ra.year, ra.round
        FROM results AS r
        JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
        WHERE ra.year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
    )
    GROUP BY driver_id, year
) AS s
JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.year  = s.year  AND ra.round = s.first_round
JOIN results AS r  ON r.driver_id = s.driver_id AND r.race_id = ra.race_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Parallel query for the last‑race constructor
SELECT s.driver_id,
       s.year,
       r.constructor_id AS last_constructor_id
FROM (
    SELECT driver_id, year, MAX(round) AS last_round
    FROM (
        SELECT r.driver_id, ra.year, ra.round
        FROM results AS r
        JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
        WHERE ra.year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
    )
    GROUP BY driver_id, year
) AS s
JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.year  = s.year  AND ra.round = s.last_round
JOIN results AS r  ON r.driver_id = s.driver_id AND r.race_id = ra.race_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: drivers who, in some 1950s season, started ≥2 rounds and had the same constructor in their first and last race that season
SELECT DISTINCT d.driver_id,
       d.forename || ' ' || d.surname AS driver_name,
       f.year,
       c.name AS constructor_name
FROM (
    -- first constructor per (driver, year)
    SELECT s.driver_id, s.year, r.constructor_id
    FROM (
        SELECT driver_id, year, MIN(round) AS first_round
        FROM (
            SELECT r.driver_id, ra.year, ra.round
            FROM results AS r
            JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
            WHERE ra.year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
        )
        GROUP BY driver_id, year
    ) AS s
    JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.year  = s.year  AND ra.round = s.first_round
    JOIN results AS r  ON r.driver_id = s.driver_id AND r.race_id = ra.race_id
) AS f
JOIN (
    -- last constructor per (driver, year)
    SELECT s.driver_id, s.year, r.constructor_id
    FROM (
        SELECT driver_id, year, MAX(round) AS last_round
        FROM (
            SELECT r.driver_id, ra.year, ra.round
            FROM results AS r
            JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
            WHERE ra.year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
        )
        GROUP BY driver_id, year
    ) AS s
    JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.year  = s.year  AND ra.round = s.last_round
    JOIN results AS r  ON r.driver_id = s.driver_id AND r.race_id = ra.race_id
) AS l
  ON f.driver_id = l.driver_id
 AND f.year      = l.year
 AND f.constructor_id = l.constructor_id   -- same constructor first & last
JOIN (
    -- verify the driver entered at least two rounds that season
    SELECT r.driver_id,
           ra.year,
           COUNT(DISTINCT ra.round) AS rounds_entered
    FROM results AS r
    JOIN races   AS ra ON ra.race_id = r.race_id
    WHERE ra.year BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
    GROUP BY r.driver_id, ra.year
    HAVING rounds_entered >= 2
) AS rr
  ON rr.driver_id = f.driver_id AND rr.year = f.year
JOIN drivers      AS d ON d.driver_id = f.driver_id
JOIN constructors AS c ON c.constructor_id = f.constructor_id
ORDER BY f.year, driver_name
LIMIT 20;
```

